    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers around **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest projection at 79.97. He is an auto-start against Paddack, bolstered further by a favorable wind forecast that adds five points to his outlook. Alongside him, **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67) presents an elite play, as he benefits from a highly favorable park environment and a targetable matchup against Sugano, allowing him to outperform several of our infielders in pure efficiency. We are also leaning heavily into our hitters facing Severino; **Luis Arraez** (66.78), **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65), and **Matt Chapman** (65.18) all project as strong starts, with the park and SP skill factors significantly elevating their floors. While **Matt Chapman** faces a slight drag due to poor historical BvP, his overall efficiency remains far too high to consider fading.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Bryson Stott**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 54.06 score. Despite a solid dynamic platoon advantage against Chandler, the optimizer favored the higher cumulative scoring profiles of our middle-of-the-order bats. Conversely, **Gavin Sheets** was an easy exclusion, falling well below our 40-point efficiency floor against a tough opponent in Gilbert, cementing his spot on the bench. We are tracking a few risks today: **Lawrence Butler** is navigating a difficult matchup against an elite arm in McDonald (2.87 xERA), which suppresses his score despite his high raw talent, and **Daulton Varsho** carries a slight risk due to the opposing catcher's elite ability to control the running game\u2014a factor we weigh heavily given our need for stolen bases. Proceed with caution as we monitor for any late-breaking lineup changes that could shift these metrics further.",
